prompt:
You are a sceptical financial analyst reviewing a forecast prepared by a colleague.

Given the following forecast for TCS (base year 2021):
{
  "strategy": "baseline",
  "base_year": 2021,
  "forecast": [
    {
      "year": 2022,
      "revenue_cr": 171689,
      "net_income_cr": 33467,
      "eps": 89.48
    },
    {
      "year": 2023,
      "revenue_cr": 179587,
      "net_income_cr": 34539,
      "eps": 92.35
    },
    {
      "year": 2024,
      "revenue_cr": 187848,
      "net_income_cr": 35650,
      "eps": 95.32
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": "FY2021 consolidated Revenue from operations grew 4.6% YoY (from \u20b91,56,949 crore in FY2020 to \u20b91,64,177 crore in FY2021), and Net Income attributable to shareholders of the Company grew approximately 0.28% YoY (from \u20b932,340 crore to \u20b932,430 crore); however, applying the adjusted PAT growth rate of 3.2% (as reported in the management overview excluding the exceptional legal provision) is more representative of underlying business momentum, so revenue is projected at 4.6% per annum and net income at 3.2% per annum. EPS is estimated by dividing projected net income by the FY2021 weighted average shares outstanding of approximately 374.01 crore shares."
}

Step 1: Identify the 3 most critical assumptions embedded in this forecast.
Step 2: For each assumption, describe one plausible scenario where it fails.
Step 3: Rate each assumption failure as Low / Medium / High risk to the forecast accuracy.
Step 4: Assign an overall confidence score from 0-100 (100 = completely certain).

Return ONLY valid JSON:
{
  "company": "<COMPANY>",
  "base_year": <YYYY>,
  "strategy": "<baseline|alt_strategy>",
  "assumptions": [
    {"assumption": "<text>", "failure_scenario": "<text>", "risk": "<Low|Medium|High>"}
  ],
  "confidence_score": <0-100>,
  "overall_critique": "<2 sentences>"
}

response:
